# Uploaded media. Two different things live under public/uploads:
#
#   1. Restaurant photos (322MB) — far too big to ship in the repo, and the
#      only set `npm run migrate:images` actually moves to Cloudinary. Run it
#      BEFORE deploying or the live site will 404 every restaurant photo.
#   2. Member document uploads — runtime, per-member, and private. Never commit.
#
# Everything else under public/uploads (staff photos, classification standards,
# annual reports, HR manuals, publications, workforce studies, newsletters) is
# fixed site content referenced by seeded database rows as plain /uploads/...
# paths. It is only ~78MB and is NOT covered by the Cloudinary migration, so it
# has to be committed — otherwise those paths 404 in production.
/public/uploads/restaurants/
/public/uploads/membership-documents/

